hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer question from one of my  face book readers Christian who runs a  company and is working with salespeople  and is asking me about compensation  so he's finding that the people who he  pays your salary to are not meeting  their sales quotas and are not doing a  good job and it's wondering if he should  move to a commission type of model so  Christian to help answer your question  good salespeople usually do like to run  on Commission they're usually very  competitive people they like closing the  deals and they know that the more they  close the more money going to make so  you definitely want to have a commission  component built in there the caveat  there is it often takes people a little  bit of time to get used to selling your  product so you want to have a buffer in  there where they can take a draw still  make money at the beginning and you know  not be out looking for other ways to  make money because they can't sell your  product so it might take three months it  might take six months just depends on  how long your sales cycle is you want to  make sure you supporting them through  that period so that when they get to you  know that Commission model they're able  to to make the money so I'd have a  commission model show them how much they  can make but be patient with them and  let them know that there's a ramp-up  period that you're going to support them  through so that they're not out you know  on the street trying to find other ways  to make money you know until they can  ramp up their sales the next thing is  I'd also make sure that I'm training  them so you're giving them all the  resources that they need to be  successful it's not just hey go out and  sell you know you're giving them a model  on how to do it hopefully you've done it  yourself before you have some experience  you can help them with or you have a  really good salesman already on stock  who can help part of the training as  well so your help support them your  champion them your believing in them and  not just saying you know go out and do  it without giving them any experience  and I'd also try to give them leads as  much as possible so if people are  contacting you by phone or email on your  website or Facebook or or there  contacting you try to give your  salespeople some leads as well so it's  not only up to them to go out and bring  in new leads if they see especially the  beginning that they can close a couple  sales it gives them some motivation  inspiration or I continue I want to do  better when I'm going to close more more  sales you know sales people there's  often writing highs and writing lows you  want to get them to those highs as  quickly as you can and there's nothing  that makes a salesperson you know more  high than closing a sale so try to get  them some warm leads as well support  their development especially at the  beginning so they get used to selling  the product and know how to do it and  they're gonna support your longer-term  so I would say move to a commission  model but just with the caveat of giving  them that base at the beginning to  support them to the transition period  and then try to give them as much  training and support and leads as  possible to make sure they're going to  be successful and be happy and help you  bury business for the long term so will  that help Christian those watching if  you liked the video please give it a  thumbs up below  I always appreciate those and I'd love  to hear what you have to think if you  want to leave a comment under the video  if you have an extra thought for  Christian or if you have a question of  your own feel free to leave a comment  under this video and we'll see you on  the next episode  you
 

